EXPERIMENT-2

AIM:- Implement a first in first out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

ALGORITHM :-
 Push(x)
 Push x into stack s1.
 Pop()
 If s2 is empty:
 Move all elements from s1 to s2.
 Remove and return the top element of s2.
 Peek()
 If s2 is empty:
 Move all elements from s1 to s2.
 Return the top element of s2.
 Empty()
 If both s1 and s2 are empty, return true.
 Otherwise, return false.

CODE:-
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1, s2;

    MyQueue() {
    }

    void push(int x) {
        s1.push(x);
    }

    int pop() {
        if (s2.empty()) {
            while (!s1.empty()) {
                s2.push(s1.top());
                s1.pop();
            }
        }
        int x = s2.top();
        s2.pop();
        return x;
    }

    int peek() {
        if (s2.empty()) {
            while (!s1.empty()) {
                s2.push(s1.top());
                s1.pop();
            }
        }
        return s2.top();
    }

    bool empty() {

        return s1.empty() && s2.empty();

    }

};


AIM:- Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a target value, return the index if the target is found. If not, return the index where it would be if it were inserted in order.

ALGORITHM:- 

1. Set low = 0 and high = n - 1.
2. Find the middle index:
    mid = low + (high - low) / 2
3. Compare arr[mid] with target:
    If arr[mid] == target, return mid.
    If arr[mid] < target, search the right half by setting low = mid + 1.
    If arr[mid] > target, search the left half by setting high = mid - 1.
4. Repeat until low > high.
5. If the target is not found, return low.
   This is the correct position where the target should be inserted. Humanity survives another binary search.

CODE:- 
class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int left = 0, right = nums.size() - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;
            else if (nums[mid] < target)
                left = mid + 1;
            else
                right = mid - 1;
        }

        return left;
    }
}; 


AIM:-  SEARCH IN ROOTED SORTED ARRAY
There is an integer array nums sorted in ascending order (with distinct values).

Prior to being passed to your function, nums is possibly left rotated at an unknown index k (1 <= k < nums.length) such that the resulting array is [nums[k], nums[k+1], ..., nums[n-1], nums[0], nums[1], ..., nums[k-1]] (0-indexed). For example, [0,1,2,4,5,6,7] might be left rotated by 3 indices and become [4,5,6,7,0,1,2].

Given the array nums after the possible rotation and an integer target, return the index of target if it is in nums, or -1 if it is not in nums.

ALGORITHM:- 
1. Set low = 0 and high = n - 1.
2. Find the middle index:
    mid = low + (high - low) / 2
3. If nums[mid] == target, return mid.
4. Check which half is sorted:
     If nums[low] <= nums[mid], the left half is sorted.
    If target lies between nums[low] and nums[mid], search left.
   Otherwise, search right.
   Otherwise, the right half is sorted.
   If target lies between nums[mid] and nums[high], search right.
   Otherwise, search left.
5. Repeat until low > high.
6. If target is not found, return -1.

CODE:- 
class Solution {
public:
    int search(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int low = 0, high = nums.size() - 1;

        while (low <= high) {
            int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;

            // Left half is sorted
            if (nums[low] <= nums[mid]) {
                if (nums[low] <= target && target < nums[mid])
                    high = mid - 1;
                else
                    low = mid + 1;
            }

            // Right half is sorted
            else {
                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[high])
                    low = mid + 1;
                else
                    high = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
};




